# ~/seo-pages IS the published artifact: the Cloudflare Pages project
# `seo-landing-pages` is a direct upload of this directory, and the sitemap
# generator walks the directory. Anything committed here becomes a live URL.
#
# Keep scratch, quarantine and tool state out of the tree.
#
# `.wrangler/` and `*.bak-*` were added by card t_e95b8a1e, in the same commit
# that deleted the 22 tracked `.wrangler/cache/*` files (wrangler's cached
# Cloudflare account id + project name) and the 3 tracked `*.bak-*` page backups
# that a now-dead pipeline had committed there. All 25 were live URLs; none were
# in the sitemap, so removing them drops no advertised loc.
#
# Both are untracked now, so no pattern below matches a tracked file. That is a
# requirement, not a nicety: a .gitignore pattern that matches an already-tracked
# file silently drops it from the next whole-directory upload (card t_0e949206
# §6). Proof at any time: `git ls-files -i -c --exclude-standard` prints nothing.

.rejected/
.quarantine/
.wrangler/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.tmp
*.orig
*.rej
*.bak-*
*.swp
*~
node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# t_495d6699: the published root must not carry internal log sinks or test
# suites either. ~/seo-pages IS the artifact (whole-tree upload to the CF Pages
# project `seo-landing-pages`, no prune), so every line a live pipeline tee'd
# into logs/ was a public URL.
#
#  * log WRITERS were relocated to ~/.hermes/logs/seo-pages/ in the same change
#    (all-sites-pipeline.sh, idle-site-pipeline.sh, seo-pipeline-runner.sh), and
#    the two readers that stat the all-sites pipeline log were re-pointed with
#    them (daily-stack-health.sh, abd-legacy-watchdog.sh).
#  * the 16 `idle-sites/*/tests/*` files are untracked but deliberately STILL ON
#    DISK: cron b292e9710c4d (2026-12-01) runs
#    `cd ~/seo-pages/idle-sites/tariff-calculator-2026 && node --test
#    tests/tariff-data.test.js`, and the tarif/calculator harnesses are run by
#    hand. They are out of HEAD, so they are out of the artifact.
#  * `tests/`, not `*/tests/`: in a .gitignore a `*` does not cross `/`, so the
#    card's literal `*/tests/` matches `idle-sites/tests/` but NOT
#    `idle-sites/<site>/tests/`. Measured with
#    `git -c core.excludesFile=<f> check-ignore --no-index -v` before choosing.
#  * no pattern below matches a tracked file -- a pattern that does silently
#    drops that file from the next whole-tree upload (card t_0e949206 §6).
#    Proof at any time: `git ls-files -i -c --exclude-standard` prints nothing.
#  * `all-sites/logs/` and `idle-sites/logs/` are redundant with `logs/`; kept so
#    the intent survives a future edit of this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
all-sites/logs/
idle-sites/logs/
tests/
